// mapdb keeps only the last value of each item, which is all restoreOnStartup
// needs -- and unlike rrd4j it can store non-numeric types.
//
// Why this file exists: rrd4j persists Number and Switch items only, so the
// four String items holding the boiler automation's target modes were never
// restored. openHAB came back with boiler_auto_control ON and all four targets
// NULL, and BoilerModeJob then logged "reads NULL" and commanded nothing every
// five minutes while the sitemap showed the automation enabled. Verified by
// the absence of boiler_auto_running_heating.rrd in the rrd4j store, where
// boiler_auto_control.rrd (a Switch) is present.
//
// Only those four are listed. Everything else whose state is configuration
// (timer_job_*, chick_01_*) is a Number or a Switch, rrd4j already restores it,
// and having both services restore the same item would put two sources on the
// same state at startup.
//
// boiler_auto_last_heating and boiler_auto_last_water are deliberately absent.
// They record where the automation last left each circuit; restoring a stale
// record would look like a change somebody made by hand and switch the
// automation off. scripts/sync-item-states.sh excludes them for the same
// reason.
//
// No Strategies block on purpose: everyChange and restoreOnStartup are built
// in, and a "default =" line inside Strategies is rejected by this openHAB and
// silently disables the whole file.

Items {
    boiler_auto_running_heating, boiler_auto_running_water, boiler_auto_idle_heating, boiler_auto_idle_water : strategy = everyChange, restoreOnStartup
}
